# Whisipedia background work (orchestrator, index builds, ad-hoc jobs started with tools/wsp-bg):
# one shared memory, swap, CPU and IO budget, so that however many jobs run at once, the desktop keeps
# the rest of the machine. The API is not in this slice; it has its own small limits.
#
# MemoryHigh throttles (reclaims) the slice before MemoryMax is reached; MemoryMax makes the kernel
# OOM-kill inside the slice only, never the desktop or the API. MemorySwapMax keeps a runaway job from
# pushing the whole machine into swap (the 2026-10-11 index build reached 21 GB RSS and 41 GB of swap).
# Override per machine with a drop-in:
#   systemctl --user edit whisipedia-background.slice
#
# Budget for a 16 GiB WSL (.wslconfig memory=16GB), audit 2026-10-12 H1. The members' own ceilings
# must fit inside this slice's MemoryHigh, or one job keeps the whole slice over it and the kernel
# throttles every member (the 8G rebuild did: lanes, orchestrator and step units stalled for hours):
#
#   machine                     16 GiB
#   API (own unit)             - 5 GiB   MemoryMax
#   kernel, page cache, shell  - 3 GiB
#   this slice                   8 GiB   MemoryMax (MemoryHigh 7 GiB)
#
#   members at once (MemoryHigh / MemoryMax):
#   orchestrator                1.5 / 2   GiB  (MemoryLow 256M: the control plane is reclaimed last)
#   fetch lanes, all together   1   / 1.5 GiB  whisipedia-background-fetch.slice (tools/wsp-bg --fetch)
#   one heavy job               3   / 4   GiB  step units, whisipedia-index.service, tools/wsp-bg
#                               ---------
#                               5.5 / 7.5 GiB  highs below the slice's 7 GiB high, maxima below its 8
#
# Only one heavy job runs at a time (the machine-wide "heavy" lock). tools/wsp-bg refuses a job whose
# MemoryMax reaches this MemoryHigh. A rebuild that needs more than 4 GiB runs with the lanes stopped:
# then up to 6G fits (2 + 6 = 8).
#
# Template: `wsp service install` renders this file (docs/runbooks/install-services.md).

[Unit]
Description=Whisipedia background work (shared memory, CPU and IO budget)

[Slice]
MemoryHigh=7G
MemoryMax=8G
MemorySwapMax=2G
CPUWeight=20
IOWeight=20
# Threads and processes of every background job together. 512 was reached 1,260 times on 2026-10-20
# (25 jobs at once: downloads, two indexers, the audit browser, the trawler): "can't start new thread"
# ended the CRS, OpenAlex and mirror fetches. A guard against a runaway job, not a working limit.
TasksMax=2048
